# MAUI MVVM

- Keep code-behind limited to view initialization and UI-only event wiring.
- Put user actions, async workflows, and state in view models using CommunityToolkit.Mvvm patterns.
- Never block the UI thread with `.Result`, `.Wait()`, synchronous image IO, or synchronous model inference.
- Use cancellation tokens for capture/pick/detect workflows where practical.
- Marshal UI updates back to the UI thread only at presentation boundaries.
- Request permissions explicitly and keep platform lifecycle implications visible in the view model or platform service.
